From 78b6474e35175ef0d8b74d3d5f55ce85fca56604 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: baristahaus <baristahaus@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 14:17:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] perf(ops): size persistent grids from the device's SM
 count

Seven sites sized one resident wave from the RTX 5090's 170 SMs (170, 510,
680, 1020, 5440). On GB10 (48 SMs) they oversubscribe by 3.5x; on an RTX PRO
6000 (188) they leave SMs idle. device_sm_count() queries the device once,
falling back to 170, and the RMSNorm prefetch gate, RoPE wave capacity, GDN
chunked output, sparse-MoE prefill, QSA score and Flash-Next MoE grouped
grids scale from it. Every one of these kernels strides its work by
gridDim.x, so the grid size changes speed only. Ported from
baristahaus/ninfer-gb10 589e4df1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PB8TNZ3p817zVAp6aH4yrz
